00:07:53.352 --> 00:07:55.060
ROMIN IRANI: It's
great to see how you've

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.730
captured user
preferences, giving them

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.040
personalized recommendations.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.370
Could you maybe share or
dive into the architecture

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.690
behind this solution too?

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.440
RUSHABH VASA: Yes.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.500
So whenever a user performs
any action on our website

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.520
or on mobile app, that action
is captured in terms of events

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.350
and we have built
our analytics logic

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.760
which helps us
capture that event

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.990
and process it on our system.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:21.070
So whenever that data is
captured on local device,

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:25.600
we pass that data from the
local device to the Cloud

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.700
using a CSV.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:32.260
That CSV is then transferred to
Cloud Storage where we extract

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.230
the data from the CSV and
store it in the Cloud Storage

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.220
for a backup.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.980
From there it goes to the
BigQuery and BigQuery,

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:42.370
we again then process that data
and query the required results

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.309
that we want.

00:08:43.309 --> 00:08:46.390
And then that results
are stored on a dashboard

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:49.000
that we have built for our
clients using the Data Studio.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.160
Also we have used a
personalized dashboard

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.860
which helps us get
more deeper insights

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.510
about the user listening
patterns and the user data.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.510
ROMIN IRANI: Thank you,
Rushabh for sharing what

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.340
